---
const foggedPhoto = 'https://images.pexels.com/photos/36732584/pexels-photo-36732584.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1800';
const condensationPhoto = 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1763976431914-5bebc66eb166?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&q=80';
interface Props { heading?: string | null; }
const { heading = 'Fogged glass: see the problem in a real window.' } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="photo-explainer">
  {heading && <figcaption class="heading">{heading}</figcaption>}
  <p class="intro">For this problem, a photograph is more useful than a technical cartoon. Start with what the glass actually looks like, then make one simple check.</p>

  <div class="photo-grid">
    <article class="photo-card failed">
      <div class="photo-wrap">
        <img src={foggedPhoto} alt="Close-up stock photograph of a window covered in heavy condensation and fogged glass." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <span class="photo-badge">A · FOGGED GLASS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-copy">
        <h3>Does it stay cloudy after you wipe the room side?</h3>
        <p>Persistent haze or moisture that remains between the panes is the classic visual sign of an insulated-glass seal problem.</p>
        <div class="check"><strong>Check:</strong><span>Wipe the room-facing surface. If the haze remains in the glass pack, it is not surface condensation.</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="photo-card surface">
      <div class="photo-wrap">
        <img src={condensationPhoto} alt="Free stock photograph of water droplets forming on a window surface." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <span class="photo-badge">B · SURFACE CONDENSATION</span>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-copy">
        <h3>Does the moisture wipe away from the glass?</h3>
        <p>Water sitting on the room-facing surface is a different condition. Indoor humidity and glass temperature can drive it.</p>
        <div class="check"><strong>Check:</strong><span>Wipe the room-facing surface. If it clears, you were looking at moisture on the surface, not inside the sealed unit.</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="quick-answer">
    <div class="qa-label">QUICK ANSWER</div>
    <div><strong>Fog that stays after wiping = investigate the insulated glass unit.</strong><span>Surface water that wipes away = start with condensation and indoor conditions.</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="photo-note"><span>Stock photography</span><span>Used to demonstrate the condition — not a Clearview installation.</span></div>
</figure>

<style>
.photo-explainer{margin:0}.heading{display:block;margin:0 0 .35rem;font-size:var(--step-2);font-weight:650;letter-spacing:var(--tracking-display);line-height:var(--leading-display)}.intro{margin:0 0 var(--space-l);max-width:74ch;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}.photo-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:var(--space-l)}.photo-card{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:4px solid var(--ink);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised);box-shadow:var(--shadow-soft)}.photo-card.failed{border-top-color:var(--danger)}.photo-card.surface{border-top-color:var(--accent)}.photo-wrap{position:relative;aspect-ratio:4/3;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper-sunk)}.photo-wrap img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center}.photo-badge{position:absolute;left:0;bottom:0;padding:.55rem .7rem;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 86%,transparent);color:var(--paper);font-size:10px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.1em}.failed .photo-badge{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--danger) 88%,transparent)}.surface .photo-badge{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent-ink) 88%,transparent)}.photo-copy{padding:var(--space-m)}.photo-copy h3{margin:0;font-size:var(--step-1);line-height:1.14}.photo-copy>p{margin:.55rem 0 0;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}.check{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:.35rem var(--space-xs);margin-top:var(--space-s);padding:.8rem .9rem;background:var(--paper-sunk);border-left:3px solid var(--ink);font-size:var(--step--1)}.failed .check{border-left-color:var(--danger)}.surface .check{border-left-color:var(--accent)}.check strong{color:var(--ink)}.check span{color:var(--ink-soft)}.quick-answer{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:var(--space-m);align-items:start;margin-top:var(--space-l);padding:var(--space-m);border:2px solid var(--ink);background:var(--paper-raised)}.qa-label{font-size:var(--step--2);font-weight:750;letter-spacing:var(--tracking-label);color:var(--ink-faint)}.quick-answer div+div{display:grid;gap:.25rem}.quick-answer strong{font-size:var(--step-0)}.quick-answer span{color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}.photo-note{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem var(--space-s);margin-top:var(--space-s);font-size:var(--step--2);color:var(--ink-faint)}.photo-note span:first-child{font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--ink-soft)}
@media(max-width:800px){.photo-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.quick-answer{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.35rem}}
</style>
